00:04:24,545 --> 00:04:30,545
Heroes come in all shapes and sizes... even rectangles.

2
00:08:49,090 --> 00:08:55,090
The Boxtrolls is a animation, comedy, family film directed by Graham Annable.

3
00:13:13,636 --> 00:13:19,636
An orphaned boy raised by underground creatures called Boxtrolls comes up from the sewers and out of
his box to save his family and the town from the evil exterminator, Archibald Snatcher.

4
00:17:38,181 --> 00:17:44,181
Snatcher (voice), played by Ben Kingsley.

5
00:22:02,727 --> 00:22:08,727
Eggs (voice), played by Isaac Hempstead Wright.

6
00:26:27,272 --> 00:26:33,272
Winnie Portley-Rind (voice), played by Elle Fanning.

7
00:30:51,818 --> 00:30:57,818
Fish / Wheels / Bucket (voice), played by Dee Bradley Baker.

8
00:35:16,363 --> 00:35:22,363
Lady Cynthia Portley-Rind (voice), played by Toni Collette.

9
00:39:40,909 --> 00:39:46,909
Lord Portley-Rind (voice), played by Jared Harris.

10
00:44:05,454 --> 00:44:11,454
The Boxtrolls is a 2014 American stop motion animated fantasy comedy
film loosely based on the 2005 novel Here Be Monsters!.

11
00:48:30,000 --> 00:48:36,000
Directed by Graham Annable and Anthony Stacchi, and produced by Laika, it features the voices of Ben Kingsley, Isaac Hempstead Wright, Elle
Fanning, Dee Bradley Baker, Steve Blum, Toni Collette, Jared Harris, Nick Frost, Richard Ayoade, Tracy Morgan, and Simon Pegg.

12
00:52:54,545 --> 00:53:00,545
Set in the fictional European country of Norvenia in the late 19th century, the film tells the story of Eggs, a human boy
raised by trash-collecting trolls, known as "Boxtrolls", as he attempts to save them from a pest exterminator.

13
00:57:19,090 --> 00:57:25,090
In 2008, Laika unveiled a slate of projects in development, including an animated
feature film adaptation of the Alan Snow novel Here Be Monsters!.

14
01:01:43,636 --> 01:01:49,636
While the animation technique was not yet decided
upon, Stacchi was set to direct the film.

15
01:06:08,181 --> 01:06:14,181
Originally focused on all five species of creatures found in the original book, producer
Travis Knight noted that the script ultimately was hollow with all the monsters.

16
01:10:32,727 --> 01:10:38,727
As the result, the team ended up focusing on the Boxtrolls as Knight thought there was
something that was really compelling about that group of characters.

17
01:14:57,272 --> 01:15:03,272
Dario Marianelli composed the film's musical score.

18
01:19:21,818 --> 01:19:27,818
The film was released in the United States on September 26, 2014, by Focus Features, and
received generally positive reviews from critics, who praised the humor and animation.

19
01:23:46,363 --> 01:23:52,363
It earned $108 million on a $60 million budget and was nominated for Best
Animated Film at the Academy Awards, the Golden Globes and the BAFTAs.

20
01:28:10,909 --> 01:28:16,909
The film explores themes of based on novel or book, parent child
relationship, stop motion, unlikely friendship, duringcreditsstinger.

21
01:32:35,454 --> 01:32:41,454
The tone is lighthearted.
